Z||000011||Steven||06-20-2001||09:45 AM||||Currently I am not a member of any club. I had went to the Michigan Fiero Club website to find out where they meet. I didn't see it anywhere on their web page, so I sent an E-mail, but got no reply. Was thinking that if the only meet somewhere way far away from me (i.e. north of Cadillac), it would not be worth it to me. However if they meet somewhere near me (say with in 20-25 miles). I would join, that way I could make it to most of the meetings.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfixit58||06-20-2001||02:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I had primed the oil pump by hand prior to installing it in the engine. After putting everything as far back togather as I could with the engine on the engine stand, I hooked up a pressure gage to the block, and used a drill motor with a socket to turn the oil pump drive shaft. Had good oil pressure. <P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>In addition to what you did, right before I fire a new motor, I always pull all sparkplugs squirt oil into each cylinder using a pump can and crank the motor over using the starter. After a few seconds of cranking, you'll notice the motor cranking faster. I then re-install the plugs and fire the motor.<BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Steven||06-20-2001||03:13 PM||||Well since I had to buy pistons for this engine rebuild, and I was using the iron heads and a 3.1 liter crank. The pistons I ordered were for the 90-92 3.1 liter "T" motor Firebird. Those have a 10cc dish in them, so I did not squirt any oil in the cylinders. But I did wipe a thin coat of GM's EOS on the cylinder walls before and after piston installation to help as much as possible. I know that the oil control rings wiped most of that away the first time the piston went up and down in the cylinder, but hey, every little bit helps.||||reg||1
